WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.635
-Orlando.
It is great to see you.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.436
Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:04.436 --> 00:00:05.638
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.440
It's always a pleasure
to see you, Jimmy.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:11.411
These un-- surreal
and new circumstances.

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:15.414
-It really is.
I'm happy that you're safe.

00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:18.518
How have you --
How is life in the quarantine?

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:22.388
-To be honest, it's been --
So, I was working a lot,

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.957
and I've found some real solace
and real kind of --

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:26.359
I think it's a reset.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.695
Everyone feels like it's a reset
that perhaps we all needed,

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:31.297
the chance to reflect
on what's important

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.766
and what we've been doing
in the --

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:38.170
And I just hope that, you know,
we can keep that --

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:43.743
That thinking can kind of
continue on past and through

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.744
once there are vaccines in place

00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:47.313
and people want to go
about their lives.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.514
I understand it's, like, just --

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:49.815
I mean,
feel incredibly blessed.

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:51.517
Obviously you're in New York,
and there are people

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.719
who probably for weeks on end

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:55.888
couldn't even get out
of their apartments, right?

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:57.990
-It was rough.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:02.362
-So I've been --
I've been feeling very grateful.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.831
Obviously, I have a little
baby girl on the way.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.299
-We got to talk about that.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:11.370
I am so excited for you
to have a baby girl.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.172
I have two girls.

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:14.674
-That's -- It's amaz--

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.342
Well, you'll have to
tell me all about it.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:19.779
I'm so excited to be --
to have a little daddy's girl.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.181
I hope -- I hope
she's going to love me

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:23.649
as much as I love her.

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:27.219
But that daddy-girl thing
and, you know...

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:28.721
That "love of your life"
feeling,

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.556
I think, is right around there,
you know?

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:33.192
-It's exactly
what everyone tells you.

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:34.794
So no spoilers from me.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.730
But it really is
love at first sight,

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.666
and then it just doesn't end,
and it's just like --

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:42.635
It's the best thing in the world

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:45.604
to just even watch them grow up
in every little thing.

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:47.640
It's just like -- It's so cute.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.276
I mean, boys -- cute, too.
Sons are great.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.711
Obviously you know that.
They're great.

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.813
But the girls.
-I got a 9-year-old boy, yeah.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:56.082
So --
-You get the little --

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:58.083
-He's got a couple
of other brothers,

00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:00.753
but this is his first sister,
so he's excited, too.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.422
So it's exciting times.
-Oh, it's -- Yeah.

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:08.427
Is that your work behind you
or is that your son's Lego work?

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:11.130
-[ Laughs ]
-Yeah!

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:14.967
-This is hours of quarantine.
Quarantining.

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:17.970
-Those are Legos?
-Those are Legos.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.306
I actually found it
kind of reassuring,

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:23.008
and, obviously --
Actually, me and Flynn

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:25.044
started with this big silver
Porsche up here.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.578
-Yeah.
-And I got so into it.

00:02:26.578 --> 00:02:28.581
He would, like, go, "Dad,
I'm going to go to bed.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:31.651
I'm like,
"Just another 15 minutes."

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.520
-"Let me stay up. Please let me
stay up a little longer."

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.188
-"Just do the next page. We'll
open the next bag. Come on."

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:38.024
-"You're my dad." Yeah. You can
stay up as long as you like.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.459
What's the green one up there?

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:42.228
What's the green one
on the top corner there?

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:46.199
-That's a Defender 90.
A Land Rover Defender 90.

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.601
-I didn't even know
they made these Legos.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.536
-Oh, man, neither did I.

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.838
Now I'm just like --
There's another Porsche.

00:02:52.838 --> 00:02:56.543
There's like a --
I mean, like this is...

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:59.345
1967 Ch--

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.947
I mean, you know, it's just fun.

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:03.482
-Wow!
-It's just hours of fun.

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:05.618
But, um --

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.020
-Well, as you were
saying before,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.488
you were filming "Carnival Row."

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.489
I think that was the last time
you were in studio with us,

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.658
filming your show
"Carnival Row."

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:15.161
Congrats. You got three
Emmy nominations, bud.

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:17.463
-Thanks, man. Yeah, no.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.198
Everyone's worked so hard
on that show.

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:22.435
It was -- The first season
was not straightforward

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:25.771
in so many ways, but I think
we really kind of brought

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:27.807
an interesting story
to the screen,

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.710
so I'm happy that
we're going back to finish.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.745
-Yeah. Congrats on the noms.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:35.882
I wanted to talk to you
about something because --

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.750
We always talk
about giving back,

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.786
and we were talking right before
we started this interview.

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:43.356
But you do a lot of work
with UNICEF.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:44.524
-Yeah.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.892
-What's your connection
with UNICEF?

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:48.795
-It's been about 10 years.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.829
Or more actually. Maybe 12.

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:53.599
But I've done --
I was trying to do basically

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:57.069
one field trip every year
just to sort of witness,

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:59.239
really, firsthand the work
that they do in the field

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.341
to save the lives
of women and children

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:04.210
in the most desperate
circumstances.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.913
And then what we will do
is video document it,

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.948
and obviously it's an NGO,
so we're trying to put

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:12.017
the messaging out to
hopefully people to support,

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:14.954
because, you know, obviously,
the world is suffering

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.656
from this global pandemic,

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:20.793
you know, and when we look
at the way we feel at home,

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.661
you kind of imagine that

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:26.332
and then times it
by 10 or even more.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:29.635
UNICEF's on the ground right now
all over the world, you know,

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:34.373
trying to get PPE equipment
to people, to vaccinate.

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:36.475
There are vaccinations
outside --

00:04:36.475 --> 00:04:39.045
I mean, water is a huge killer.

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:42.581
So they need to inoculate for
children under the age of 2.

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:43.783
Diarrhea is a huge killer.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.951
There are so many huge issues.

00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:48.454
Then you add
that COVID element on top.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.357
So it's something that
is very close to my heart,

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:53.192
you know, to see these children,

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.494
and I've worked with them
so many times.

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:59.398 line:0%
And, you know, they're always
looking for support.

00:04:59.398 --> 00:05:01.867 line:0%
UNICEF's always looking
for that support because --

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:04.503 line:0%
Obviously,
it's so challenging at home,

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:06.939 line:0%
but it's also, you know,
having the foresight

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.907 line:0%
that we are a global community.

00:05:08.907 --> 00:05:11.177
We are a global community.

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:14.113
And when one part of
that community is suffering,

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.714
the whole -- the whole suffers.

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:18.650
And just kind of grappling
with that idea

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.053
is sometimes challenging,
but it's something

00:05:21.053 --> 00:05:23.823
that's so, you know, amazing
when you see it.

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:26.359
-Well, thanks so much
for talking about it

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:28.527
and getting people
talking about it.

00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:29.729
-Thanks for asking, honestly.

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:31.297
I've been watching your show
a little bit,

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:32.999
and it's great to see
that you guys are kind of

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:35.067
highlighting people's causes

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:38.071
'cause it's something that --
We all want to have something

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:40.206
that we can do
to give back in some way.

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:42.075
-That's the least
we can do, right?

